  "reason": "With no prior experiments completed, there is no evidence to guide exploitation; the priority is establishing a clear, interpretable baseline. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the simplest viable configuration: a single modality, a single profile, and the most straightforward linear encoder (PCA). It carries minimal implementation risk and isolates the core classification task without confounding from fusion, aggregation, or learned encoders. This baseline performance will serve as the reference floor against which we can measure the incremental contribution of each design axis (profile setting, encoder choice, image modality, aggregation, fusion) in subsequent experiments. Starting at the simplest corner of the design space allows each follow-up to change one dimension at a time, maximizing the information gained per experiment under the limited budget."
}

